    "schema_diff_summary": "history.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add undo_depth on impl History. Keep it public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is self.undo.len(). Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch can_undo, can_redo, is_modified, record, or undo. The existing test redo_onto_the_saved_depth_sets_the_seal stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test undo_depth_tracks_one_record uses the existing record_insert helper. A new History has depth 0. After one record_insert the depth is 1. After undo the depth is 0. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
